  {
   "id": "ex1",
   "type": "example",
   "problem": {
    "en": "A firm's cost is C = x³/3 − 7x² + 111x + 50 and demand is x = 100 − p. Find the output for maximum profit."
   },
   "steps": [
    {
     "en": "R = px = (100 − x)x = 100x − x²."
    },
    {
     "en": "P = R − C = −x³/3 + 6x² − 11x − 50; P′ = −x² + 12x − 11 = 0 gives x = 1 or 11."
    },
    {
     "en": "P″ = −2x + 12: at x = 11, P″ = −10 < 0 (maximum)."
    }
   ],
   "answer": {
    "en": "x = 11 units"
   },
   "narration": {
    "en": "Let us solve this together. A firm's cost is C = x³/3 − 7x² + 111x + 50 and demand is x = 100 − p. Find the output for maximum profit."
   }
  },
